SPARTA (24 Sep 2025)
Running on 1 MPI task(s)
################################################################################
# thermal gas in a 3d box with tabulated collision cross sections
# particles reflect off global box boundaries
#
# the cross section table was generated from the VHS parameters in
# data/ar.vss, so this run reproduces examples/collide/in.collide
#
# Note:
#  - The "comm/sort” option to the “global” command is used to match MPI runs.
#  - The “twopass” option is used to match Kokkos runs.
# The "comm/sort" and "twopass" options should not be used for production runs.
################################################################################

seed	    	    12345
dimension   	    3
global              gridcut 1.0e-5 comm/sort yes

boundary	    rr rr rr

create_box  	    0 0.0001 0 0.0001 0 0.0001
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (0.0001 0.0001 0.0001)
create_grid 	    10 10 10
Created 1000 child grid cells
  CPU time = 0.00115085 secs
  create/ghost percent = 85.664 14.336

balance_grid        rcb part
Balance grid migrated 0 cells
  CPU time = 0.000198841 secs
  reassign/sort/migrate/ghost percent = 39.2086 0.479616 10.0719 50.2398

species		    ar.species Ar
mixture		    air Ar vstream 0.0 0.0 0.0 temp 273.15

global              nrho 7.07043E22
global              fnum 7.07043E6

collide		    table air ar.tab.vss linear 64
Cross section table AR_AR_VHS from ar_ar.tab:
  200 values, E = 0.0001 to 1000 eV, max sigma = 3.181e-18 m^2, log-log interpolation
  1489 bins, 64 per factor of 2 in energy, reproduces input to 0.000462%

create_particles    air n 10000 twopass
Created 10000 particles
  CPU time = 0.00239801 secs

stats		    100
compute             temp temp
stats_style	    step cpu np nattempt ncoll c_temp

timestep 	    7.00E-9
run 		    1000
